flowchart LR
    accTitle: M4 trust boundaries and attack shapes
    accDescr: Owner instruction becomes signed history, crosses the store transport boundary, and is verified by every host before propagation gates determine apply or hold. Each stolen-key, replay, and hub-credential attempt has its own dashed path to a stopping gate and a named residual.
    subgraph Owner
        O["1 · Instruction<br/>Owner chain"]
    end
    subgraph Host["Enrolled host (one machine)"]
        K["2 · Key<br/>Signing key"] --> S["3 · Sign<br/>Signed history"]
        T["Root-owned roster / refs"]
    end
    subgraph Hub["Store boundary (transport only)"]
        R[("4 · Store<br/>Private repository")]
    end
    subgraph Fleet["Every other host"]
        V["5 · Verify<br/>Parent-position ratchet"]
        G["6 · Gate<br/>Scope · soak · canary · ancestry"]
        O2["7 · Outcome<br/>Apply or hold + alert"]
    end
    O --> K
    S --> R --> V --> G --> O2
    T -.-> V
    O2 -->|apply| A2["Apply after evidence"]
    O2 -->|hold| HD["Hold + named alert"]
    AK["ATTEMPT A<br/>stolen machine key"] -.-> GA["A gate<br/>parent / class scope"]
    GA --> RA["A residual<br/>bounded authority until retirement"]
    RP["ATTEMPT B<br/>replay / downgrade"] -.-> GB["B gate<br/>ancestry / high-water"]
    GB --> RB["B residual<br/>offline persistence"]
    HC["ATTEMPT C<br/>hub credential theft"] -.-> GC["C gate<br/>store transports only"]
    GC --> RC["C residual<br/>disclosure / availability"]
    G -.-> AG["8 · Contain<br/>gate stops each attempt"]
    AG --> RES["9 · Residual<br/>operator-held remainder"]
